# What NOT to send to Docker when building.
#
# Before it runs a single instruction, Docker copies the whole directory to the
# engine. Anything listed here is left behind. Two reasons to care: a build that
# ships a hundred thousand files in node_modules is slow every time, and a file
# that is copied in can end up in the finished image whether you meant it or not.
#
# The rule of thumb is that anything which can be rebuilt, and anything private,
# should be in this file.

# Rebuilt inside the image, and enormous
**/node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/.svelte-kit/
web/build/

# Generated by the image itself, from the tracked data dictionary
data/out/

# Local Python environments and their caches
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# A database built during the image build. Copying a local one in would ship
# whatever happened to be on the machine that ran the build.
api/pmsc.db

# Test output and screenshots
web/tests/*.png

# Editor and OS clutter
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Never
.env
.env.*
.git/
